  "url": "/ShowUserReviews-g495037-d1483551-r992571459-Discovery_Parks_Robe-Robe_South_Australia.html",
  "title": "3 and a half stars!",
  "language": "en",
  "originalLanguage": "en",
  "roomTip": null,
  "text": "We were a group of 6 adults staying in three deluxe waterfront cabins.  The cabins themselves were lovely - well-appointed, clean and spacious - with large balconies fronting the road and parking area.  Be aware that “waterfront” does not mean “water view”, unless you scramble onto the roof.  That disappointment was added to by the lack of beach access at the northern end of the park where we were (there’s a low-ish brick wall in front of the cabins, but my vaulting days are well and truly over), meaning that we had to use the main entrance to visit the beach.  We all had trouble with the WiFi - intermittent at best.  We liked the park’s location, about 2 and a half kilometres from town and very quiet.  Highly recommend the Robe Coastal Trail, which starts just south of the park and will be a 12-kilometre loop when finished.",
